{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794443070,"nonce":"ouKaKqbw9s6snIcGJrIymB4ktag=","message":"Committed as f231f0e, not pushed.\n\nText to and from a lent function: `impl Fn(\u0026str, i32) -\u003e Result\u003cString, E\u003e`.\n\n- Going to the function, text is a `Slice` at the boundary, borrowed for the call. The hxcpp trampoline makes a `::String` of it (`hxn::text`). HashLink's native code cannot make a `String`, so its trampoline copies the text into the VM's bytes as UTF-16, boxes those (`hxn_hl::box_bytes`, new), and the Haxe wrapper makes the string with `String.fromUCS2` before calling the user's function. The wrapper's native type therefore differs between the two runtimes (`hl.Bytes` against `String`), and the emitters now say which they write for.\n- Coming back, text is a `Buf` the host fills. `Buf` carries its own `free`, which until now only the library set; here the host sets it. On hxcpp `hxn::give_text` copies the string's UTF-8 into `malloc`ed memory with `free` as the release; on HashLink the trampoline, which is Rust in the adapter, reads the returned `String` and writes a `Buf` from a `Vec`. Either way the library reads the bytes and frees them, and holds nothing of the collector's after the function returns.\n- A shape with text is not called through `Callback::invoke`: a borrowed argument is a higher-ranked function pointer type, which `invoke`'s generic parameters do not match. The adapter writes a small function a shape (`call_si_to_s`) over `Callback::func`.\n- A function that gives text cannot give null: null is how its wrapper reports a throw. The wrapper throws \"a function lent to a library returned null\" for it.\n- Text that is not valid UTF-8 or UTF-16 fails the call with `Status::ENCODING`.\n\nFixture: `Counter::described`, `words`, `titled`.\n\nWeighed and not done: handing the library a slice of the returned string's own bytes, to save the copy. It would have to stay valid after the trampoline's frame is gone, which holds on hxcpp only because nothing collects before the library copies it; the buffer says who owns what.\n\nStill not passed to or from a lent function: bytes and objects.\n\nRun: tests/counter/run.sh gen-hl on Ash (hybrid, jit, interp, three times each) and stock HashLink on the NUC, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, gen-wasm and gen-emcc; the hand-written hl, cpp and emcc modes, since hxn-hl changed; tests/examples/run.sh on Ash and hxcpp. Under Emscripten hxcpp counts a string in bytes, which one check of the fixture had to stop depending on. Not run: Windows and hxcpp on Linux.","files":null}]}